{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GAL",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stand fast therefore in the liberty with which Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I Paul say to you, that if ye be circumcised, Christ will profit you nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I testify again to every man that is circumcised, that he is a debtor to do the whole law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Christ is become of no effect to you, whoever of you are justified by the law; ye have fallen from grace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we through the Spirit wait for the hope of righteousness by faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in Jesus Christ neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye did run well, who hindered you that ye should not obey the truth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This persuasion ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not from him that calleth you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have confidence in you through the Lord, that ye will be no otherwise minded: but he that troubleth you shall bear his judgment, whoever he may be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I, brethren, if I yet preach circumcision, why do I yet suffer persecution? then hath the offense of the cross ceased.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would they were even cut off who trouble you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For, brethren, ye have been called to liberty; only ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "use",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all the law is fulfilled in one word, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in this, Thou shalt love thy neighbor as thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one by another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye will not fulfill the lust of the flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other; so that ye cannot do the things that ye would.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if ye are led by the Spirit, ye are not under the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revelings, and such like: of which I tell you before, as I have also told ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in time past, that they who do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, long-suffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that are Christ's have crucified the flesh, with the affections and lusts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GAL.5.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GAL.5.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us not be desirous of vain-glory, provoking one another, envying one another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
